invariant: INV-28
file: tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the client's tcp-nonblocking driver reaches for the socket to wait for the
  rest of a message instead of returning and letting the caller bring
  more bytes. That is the one thing the mode exists to avoid: the
  callback runs inside an event loop with no thread to park. It is
  srv-tcp-nonblocking-out-blocks-the-caller on the other side of the connection, and
  the handshake still completes, so only a test whose recv fails the run
  catches it.

--- old
    size_t off = 0;
    for (;;) {
--- new
    size_t off = 0;
    uint8_t probe[1];
    (void)r->t.cfg.recv(r->t.cfg.io, probe, sizeof probe);
    for (;;) {
